Well, then; it's hard to judge in this case. I typically try to not
enchant the staff, rahter save the scroll for an artifact or for a
bunch of good daggers. Problem is that you may die with an unused
scroll in your inventory.

If you're yet quite inexperienced I probably better suggest to read
the scroll on the staff, but you may as well feel confident enough
already to have some feeling WRT criticality of the situations in a
NH game, whether to better read the scroll, or whether you are good
enough with your offensive spells and with your defensive tactics so
that you can delay reading.

> I've also been sacrificing but receiving no message...?

It can require quite some time, or an artifact can come immediately;
be persistent. But take care that you have enough food, and mind
that you should not get in trouble shortly after having been granted
a gift because your god might not react to an emergency prayer for
help - offer some more until you get a feeling of reconcilliation.

